---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A modal side sheet (the default <code>variant</code>) opens a native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>
  in the browser’s top layer with a scrim. The page behind it is inert and doesn’t scroll, focus
  moves to the element with <code>autofocus</code> inside it, and returns to where it was when
  the sheet closes. Escape and a scrim click close it; set <code>no-light-dismiss</code> to keep
  it open on scrim clicks.
</p>
<p>
  Set <code>heading</code> to show a header with a close button; the heading also names the
  sheet for screen readers. Without a heading, give it a <code>label</code>. Set
  <code>hide-close</code> to drop the close button when the content has its own way out.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button id='show-side-sheet-end'>Open filters</wc-button>
  <wc-button id='show-side-sheet-start' variant='outlined'>Open from the start</wc-button>

  <wc-side-sheet id='side-sheet-end' heading='Filters'>
    <p style='margin: 0 0 1rem;'>Narrow the list of 128 products.</p>
    <wc-checkbox autofocus>In stock only</wc-checkbox>
    <wc-checkbox>Free shipping</wc-checkbox>
    <div style='margin-top: 1.5rem;'>
      <wc-button data-close-side-sheet>Apply</wc-button>
    </div>
  </wc-side-sheet>

  <wc-side-sheet id='side-sheet-start' heading='Projects' placement='start'>
    <p style='margin: 0;'>
      <code>placement="start"</code> opens from the left edge in left-to-right pages and from the
      right edge in right-to-left pages.
    </p>
  </wc-side-sheet>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#show-side-sheet-end').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelector('#side-sheet-end').show();
    });
    document.querySelector('#show-side-sheet-start').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelector('#side-sheet-start').show();
    });
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-close-side-sheet]').forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => button.closest('wc-side-sheet').hide());
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Standard variant</h3>
<p>
  <code>variant="standard"</code> opens the sheet with <code>dialog.show()</code>: it isn’t
  modal, has no scrim and stays in the page flow, so place it in a flex row beside the content.
  It doesn’t trap focus, lock scrolling or close on Escape.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-button id='toggle-standard-side-sheet' variant='outlined'>Toggle details</wc-button>
  <div
    style='display: flex; height: 240px; margin-top: 1rem; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); border-radius: var(--shape-corner-medium);'
  >
    <p style='flex: 1; margin: 0; padding: 1rem;'>Page content</p>
    <wc-side-sheet id='standard-side-sheet' variant='standard' heading='Details' open>
      Supplemental content that sits beside the page.
    </wc-side-sheet>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#toggle-standard-side-sheet').addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelector('#standard-side-sheet').toggle();
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Events</h3>
<p>
  The sheet fires <code>open</code> when it opens and <code>close</code> when it closes, with
  <code>detail.reason</code>: <code>'escape'</code>, <code>'light-dismiss'</code> (a scrim
  click), <code>'action'</code> (the close button) or <code>'api'</code> (<code>hide()</code>).
</p>
